  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Page No.# 1/6 vs The State Of Assam on 9 December, 2024 Page No.# 1 Gahc010007302010 2024:Gau-As:12581 The Gauhati High Court (High Court Of Assam, Nagaland, Mizoram And Arunachal Pradesh) Case No. : Crl.Rev.P./361/2010 Gaurav Deorah and Anr S/O Sri Ram Gopal Deorah 2: Sri Ram Gopal Deorah S/O Lt. Basudeo Deorah Both R/O T.R. Phookan Road Fancy Bazar Ghy-1 Dist. Kamrup Assam Versus The State Of Assam Advocate for the Petitioner : Mr.B Deka, Mr.J M Choudhury,Mr.D K Kothari,Mrr K Mour,Mr.D Talukdar Advocate for the Respondent : Pp, Assam, ,,, Before Hon'Ble Mr Justice Arun Dev Choudhury For the Petitioner : Mr. Y. Kothari, Advocate. For the Respondents : Mr. B. Sarma, App. Date of Hearing : 09.12.2024 Page No.# 2/6 Date of Judgement : 09.12.2024 Page No.# 1/6 vs The State Of Assam on 9 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/179026814/ 1 Judgment & Order (Oral) 1.",
    "facts": "2. The present criminal revision petition under Section 397/401 read with Section 482 of Cr.P.C., 1973 is filed assailing a Judgment and Order dated 07.01.2010 passed by the learned Sub Divisional Judicial Magistrate No.II (Sadar), Kamrup, Guwahati in C.R.Case No. 82 c/1999, whereby the accused petitioners were convicted under Section 7/16 of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 (hereinafter referred to as Act, 1954) and petitioners were sentenced to undergo Simple Imprisonment for 6 (six) months each and to pay a fine of Rs. 10,000/- each and in default to pay fine, Simple Imprisonment for another 1 (one) month. However, in terms of Section 52 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (hereinafter referred to as Act, 2006), the punishment Page No.# 3/6 prescribed is now only fine upto Rs. 3 lakhs and therefore he submits that the petitioners should also get benefit of the aforesaid principle of law laid down by the Hon'ble Apex Court. The learned counsel, however, has confined his argument to the sentence only. The basic allegation in the complaint is to the effect that as per the Public Analyst Report dated 18.11.1988, refined vegetable oil which is sold by the petitioner is rancid and does not conform to the standard and the same is misbranded. Such materials were seized from the possession of the petitioners.",
    "arguments": "5. It is submitted by the learned counsel for the petitioners that though three of the accused person including the accused No. 3 i.e. National Co- operative Consumer's Federation of India Ltd were convicted, however, the accused No. 3, did not prefer any appeal and paid the fine."
  },
